/**
  @page gallery Gallery
  @brief Computed fields, evolving designs and fitted meshes.

  The figures link to tutorials with the mathematical problem, executable
  source, output files and numerical checks. Colors and geometry come from
  the computed output described on those pages.

  @tableofcontents
  @m_footernavigation

  @section gallery-pdes Partial differential equations

  @subsection gallery-pdes-poisson Poisson equation

  @image html PDEs/Poisson.png width=360px

  Scalar diffusion on the unit square with homogeneous Dirichlet data.
  Continuous @f$P_1@f$ elements supply the field, and CG solves the symmetric
  positive-definite system.

  @ref examples-pdes-poisson "Open tutorial →"

  @subsection gallery-pdes-elasticity Linear elasticity

  @image html Elasticity.png width=360px

  A clamped beam with end traction, vector-valued @f$P_1@f$ displacement and
  the linear elastic strain–stress relation. The displayed deformation is
  amplified for inspection.

  @ref examples-pdes-elasticity "Open tutorial →"

  @subsection gallery-pdes-helmholtz Helmholtz equation

  @image html PDEs/Helmholtz.png width=360px

  A manufactured complex wave field with prescribed boundary values.
  Real and imaginary parts are displayed separately after the complex solve.

  @ref examples-pdes-helmholtz "Open tutorial →"

  @subsection gallery-pdes-stokes Stokes equations

  @image html PDEs/Stokes.png width=360px

  Viscous cavity flow with a regularized lid, mixed velocity–pressure spaces
  and a zero-mean pressure constraint.

  @ref examples-pdes-stokes "Open tutorial →"

  @subsection gallery-pdes-navierstokes Navier–Stokes equations

  @image html PDEs/NavierStokes.png width=360px

  Transient flow driven by a horizontally moving lid patch. Taylor–Hood
  elements and semi-implicit Oseen steps resolve the velocity and pressure.
  The tutorial includes the computed animation.

  @ref examples-pdes-navierstokes "Open tutorial and video →"

  @subsection gallery-pdes-periodic Periodic Poisson equation

  @image html PDEs/Periodic.png width=360px

  A periodic scalar field with identified boundary degrees of freedom and
  a mean-value constraint fixing the constant mode.

  @ref examples-pdes-periodic "Open tutorial →"

  @subsection gallery-pdes-surface Reaction–diffusion on a surface

  @image html PDEs/SurfaceMesh.png width=360px

  A reaction–diffusion field on a triangulated approximation of the unit
  sphere. Tangential gradients and surface measure enter the variational form.

  @ref examples-pdes-surfacemesh "Open tutorial →"

  @subsection gallery-pdes-dg Discontinuous Galerkin diffusion

  @image html DGPoisson.png width=360px

  A symmetric interior-penalty method with independent affine coefficients
  on each triangle. The tutorial checks a nonzero Dirichlet patch and
  measured convergence under refinement.

  @ref examples-pdes-dg-poisson "Open tutorial →"

  @section gallery-optimization Optimization

  @subsection gallery-shapeopt-cantilever Boundary-deformation cantilever

  @image html SimpleCantilever.png width=360px

  Initial and updated domains for compliance minimization with an area
  penalty. A regularized shape derivative drives boundary displacement and
  MMG maintains the mesh between updates.

  @ref examples-shapeoptimization-simple_cantilever "Open tutorial →"

  @subsection gallery-shapeopt-levelset Level-set cantilever

  @image html LevelSetCantilever.png width=360px

  A transported level set and body-fitted elasticity solve. The page records
  the fixed-step objective history and the measured mesh-quality limitation.

  @ref examples-shapeoptimization-levelset_cantilever "Open tutorial →"

  @subsection gallery-density-temp Thermal material distribution

  @image html SIMPTemperatureMinimization.png width=360px

  A SIMP conductivity field updated using the state, adjoint and regularized
  design gradient. The objective combines mean temperature and a material penalty.

  @ref examples-density_optimization-simp_temperature_minimization "Open tutorial →"

  @section gallery-fitting Geometry and distance fields

  @subsection gallery-fitting-swift Interface fitting

  @image html SWIFTCurvedFitting-moved.png width=360px

  Quadratic fitting of a four-lobe target. The reference mesh is retained
  while all output geometry nodes receive the solved displacement.

  @ref guides-swift "Open SWIFT guide →"

  @subsection gallery-fitting-fmm Arrival-time propagation

  @image html FMMArrival.png width=360px

  Unit-speed propagation from a central vertex. The tutorial compares the
  computed field with analytic distance at three mesh resolutions.

  @ref examples-eikonal-fmm "Open tutorial →"

  @subsection gallery-fitting-distance Distance normalization

  @image html DistanceNormalization-normalized.png width=360px

  A signed Poisson potential normalized around three disks. An analytic
  reference exposes the geometric and normalization errors.

  @ref examples-distance-normalization "Open tutorial →"

  @section gallery-see-also Continue

  - @ref examples-index — Choose a numerical problem.
  - @ref guides-io — Export and inspect computed fields.
  - @ref examples-mmg-index — Prepare and adapt mesh geometry.
*/
